From: knapcio <knapcio@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:31:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] DFlash2 drafter body and MTP eh_proj on INT4 g32
 records behind G6_DFL_BODY_I4 / G6_MTP_EHPROJ_I4

The drafter's body GEMVs (fc, per layer kv / aconv / q / o / mconv / gu / down) and the MTP draft's eh_proj
are rebound at boot to INT4 g32 copies of their MXFP8 records (k_mx_to_i4, DEC_I4PAIR repack for the GEMV's
ks), same splits: 382 MB instead of 701 MB per draft step, eh_proj 10.6 instead of 19.5 MB under
G6_MTP_SPLIT. Drafts only; default 0 leaves the engine as it was.

dflreplay replays a G6_DFL_DUMP through the MXFP8 and the INT4 drafter on one GPU (matched contexts):
per-position draft agreement, acceptance against the committed tokens, and a timed body-GEMV graph.
dhead_i4_test covers the drafter shapes and times them (--time-dfl).
